{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`. Context data: `K`, `N`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: replaced the manual marginalized Bernoulli-mixture likelihood implemented with `target += log_sum_exp(...)` by the equivalent built-in sampling statement `y ~ bernoulli(dot_product(cluster_weight, cluster_prob))`. For binary observations, `sum_k cluster_weight[k] * Bernoulli(y | cluster_prob[k])` equals `Bernoulli(y | dot_product(cluster_weight, cluster_prob))`, so the posterior density is unchanged. No data fields were added or modified.
","model_safe_stan":"// ForestDB translation: Nested Chinese Restaurant Process
data {
  int<lower=1> K;
  int<lower=1> N;
  array[N] int<lower=0, upper=1> y;
}
parameters {
  simplex[K] cluster_weight;
  vector<lower=0, upper=1>[K] cluster_prob;
}
model {
  cluster_weight ~ dirichlet(rep_vector(1.0 / K, K));
  cluster_prob ~ beta(1, 1);
  y ~ bernoulli(dot_product(cluster_weight, cluster_prob));
}
generated quantities {
  int<lower=1, upper=K> cluster = categorical_rng(cluster_weight);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"K":2,"N":3,"y":[1,0,1]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
